Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Persona files use the 5-section body shape mirroring the
    primary-persona's `to_agent_md` projection precedent
    (framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/agent_md.py:
    Identity anchor + Persona prompt with Role/Voice/...).
  - Frontmatter `tools:` for loam-researcher restricts to
    Read/Grep/Glob/WebFetch/WebSearch (read-only); for loam-
    reviewer restricts to Read/Grep/Glob/Bash (review tools +
    read-only Bash for git operations). Other personas inherit
    full surface (Edit/Write/Bash needed for build/docs/plan-
    author surfaces).
  - Symlinks (not copies) so plugin updates propagate without
    re-bootstrap. Symlink target is the absolute resolved path of
    the plugin agent file.
  - Plugin-root resolver checks canonical layout first
    (<workspace>/plugins/), then derived-workspace layout
    (<workspace>/framework/plugins/) per the D-architecture
    nesting. Returns None when neither present (no error; simply
    no plugin agents to register).
  - Idempotence: existing symlinks (any target) are left alone
    per operator-precedence; non-symlink collisions raise
    PluginAgentCollisionError so operator resolves explicitly.
  - PluginAgentCollisionError uses ERR_HANDS_OFF_INTERNAL
    (-32099) error code, matching the existing scaffold-internal
    error code convention per first_run_scaffold.py:75.
  - Tests are parametrized over the 5 personas (single test
    file: 23 tests; one parametrized fn × 5 personas + 8
    named-references tests) following the v0.1.3 SKILL.md AC.LSK
    precedent. Two scaffold tests cover AC.PERSONAS.6 (10 cases)
    + AC.PERSONAS.7 (4 cases) separately.
  - No edit to `plugins/dev-sdlc/dev-mode-manifest.yaml` (the
    agents/ directory is plugin-tree-internal; admission to the
    DEV-MODE auto-load partition is out-of-fence per sub-plan §7).

